p and on the flop. This passivity suggests they likely have a weak hand, but it could still easily beat 5-high (e.g., any pair or even Ace-high). \n\nPromising moves:\n1.  **Check (0):** This is the most logical move. It costs zero chips and allows us to see the river card. Since we have very little chance of winning at showdown without significant improvement (which is unlikely), keeping the pot small and not risking chips is optimal.\n2.  **Bet (Raise):** Betting might induce a fold if the opponent has absolutely nothing, but given the presence of high cards (K, J) on the board, it is very likely the opponent has connected in some way or has a high card that beats a 5. A bluff here is high risk with low equity.\n\nReason:\nWith 5-high and no realistic draws on the turn, the hand has almost zero showdown value. The opponent is checking, allowing us to check back for free. There is no incentive to bloat the pot or bluff when the likelihood of being called by a better hand (even High Card Ace or a small pair) is high.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
